      "doctor_question": "Hello, I am Dr. Smith. Could you please tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S009",
      "patient_response": "Hi Dr. Smith. Well, I guess what finally made me ask for help is that I just keep forgetting these little things that I normally handle without an issue. Like, I'll forget to return phone calls, or I'll completely forget to turn in a registration form. Actually, that form was for my niece's baking class, and my sister was so annoyed with me because they almost lost their spot. She always gets like that, though. Even when we were kids, if I forgot to bring her hairbrush back or something, she would just hold a grudge for days. She has this really long, thick curly hair, so I guess I get why she was protective of her stuff, but still. \n\nUm... wait, what was I saying? Oh, right, why I'm here. Yeah, just forgetting stuff. Like even just telling myself I need to stop for an errand on the way home from work, and then I just completely drive right past the store and go straight home. I don't know, it's just been really bothering me lately.",
