    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you struggled with this kind of forgetfulness and difficulty staying on top of tasks since you were a child, or is this a relatively new change for you?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, it's definitely not new. Even back in elementary school, I was always that kid who forgot permission slips, or I'd completely lose my homework at the bottom of my backpack. Actually, I had this amazing Lisa Frank backpack in fourth grade—it had those neon tigers on it, you know? I begged my mom for it for literally months because all the girls in my class had them. But then I left a banana in the front pocket over a long weekend and it got totally smushed and ruined the fabric. It smelled so bad for the rest of the year, and my mom was so mad at me because they were kind of expensive. \n\nBut yeah, she... um, she and my teachers always had to remind me step by step to finish any of my school projects. Like if we had a science fair thing, I'd get stuck just decorating the title on the poster board and forget to actually do the rest of it. I'd just get so wrapped up in the glitter and the markers, and then my mom would have to sit at the kitchen table and walk me through every single step just to get it done by morning. \n\nWait, did you ask about school or work? I'm sorry, I totally lost my train of thought.",
