    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often find yourself acting or speaking without thinking, such as interrupting others during conversations or making impulsive decisions?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, not really? I mean, I don't think I'm impulsive or anything. I don't really interrupt people, at least I try not to. I know how annoying that is. My ex-boyfriend used to do that all the time. Like, I'd be right in the middle of telling him about a really stressful phone call I had at work—because dealing with some of our clients is just exhausting, they'll call and complain about literally anything—and he would just cut me off to talk about his fantasy football team. It was so rude! I mean, I don't even understand fantasy football. Why would you spend hours obsessing over stats for players who aren't even on the same real-life team? It just seems like a lot of extra math for no reason. I was never very good at math, honestly. In high school, I had to take algebra twice because the first teacher I had just mumbled into the chalkboard the whole time. \n\nOh, sorry, what were we talking about? Did you ask about interrupting people? Yeah, no, I don't really do that. I usually just kind of zone out if I'm not talking, to be honest.",
